cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use arris-gym in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "arris-gym: exact, deterministic scoring of CAD-code models on the arris kernel"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sergienko
    given-names: Sergei
repository-code: "https://github.com/arris-labs/arris-gym"
url: "https://github.com/arris-labs/arris-gym"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  arris-gym is a Python library that runs model-written CAD programs on the
  arris B-Rep kernel in a sandbox, returns a typed outcome for every program,
  and scores the result against a target exactly and deterministically,
  counting every failure. It speaks arris.build and a CadQuery-compatible
  subset, so existing benchmarks and models can run on it.
keywords:
  - CAD
  - B-Rep
  - CadQuery
  - code generation
  - benchmark
  - reinforcement learning
